// Chain Fusion signer for Internet Identity users (Path A): an ICP canister holds no Solana keys of its own. Each user's
// Solana address is a threshold Ed25519 public key (`schnorr_public_key`, algorithm ed25519) derived from their
// principal, and transactions are signed with `sign_with_schnorr` under the same derivation path.
//
// The canister is canisters/solana_signer (Motoko); its own copy of this interface, canisters/solana_signer/
// solana_signer.did, is what `mops build` checks it against. The app's client (chainFusionSigner.ts, solanaSignerIdl.ts)
// calls get_solana_address and sign_solana_transaction.
//
// Security contract, enforced by the canister (the frontend cannot):
//   * sign_solana_transaction derives the key ONLY from msg.caller. It never signs with a key chosen by an argument.
//     Anonymous callers are refused.
//   * Its second argument is the 32-byte Solana public key the client expects to sign as. The canister derives the
//     caller's key, compares, and refuses a mismatch before requesting any signature, so a client can never sign as
//     someone else, and a stale address is caught instead of producing a signature for the wrong account.
//   * Its first argument is the serialized Solana transaction message (the bytes Ed25519 signs over, 1 to 1232 bytes);
//     the result is the 64-byte signature. Callers are rate-limited, per caller and globally (every signature costs
//     cycles).
//   * get_solana_address is an update call: deriving a key calls the management canister, which a query can't. It
//     only reads a public key, so any principal can be looked up. lookup_solana_address is the query for an address
//     the canister has already derived.
// Refusals are rejects whose message says why.
type Limits = record { per_caller_per_minute : nat; global_per_minute : nat };
type ConfigUpdate = record { key_name : opt text; signing_paused : opt bool; limits : opt Limits };
type Status = record {
  key_name : text;
  signing_paused : bool;
  limits : Limits;
  known_addresses : nat;
  signatures_issued : nat;
};
service : {
  get_solana_address : (principal) -> (text);
  lookup_solana_address : (principal) -> (opt text) query;
  sign_solana_transaction : (blob, vec nat8) -> (blob);
  configure : (ConfigUpdate) -> ();
  status : () -> (Status) query;
}
